  "description": "The 158 Poor Law Unions of Ireland at the census of 2 Apr 1911: 112 in one county, 38 in two and 8 in three. Each union is built by grouping the 3,673 District Electoral Divisions of the 1911 census by the union they were in, from the county districts in each county volume's Table VI and the DED numbers in Table VII (which runs union by union). The DED map is Phelim Birch's and Paddy Matthews's (Leinster 29 Apr 1910, Connacht and Munster 1907, Ulster as on census day). Every union's DED areas add up to the acreage printed in the 1911 General Report Table 51 (152 of 158 within 0.01%), and its DED populations to the printed population. Each union carries its census acreage and population; quote census_acres rather than the map area, which takes in large lakes and estuaries the census leaves out. The King's County DEDs are placed from Table VI of the 1911 King's County volume.",
